                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="903-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_xy.png" width=27 height=27 alt="X/Y Stereo" title="X/Y Stereo" ></span>MXL V63M Stereo</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    X/Y Stereo Condenser Stereo Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The V63M Stereo is an XY-stereo FET condenser microphone.</p><p>Although it shares a name and a body style with the V63M, this mic is not another large-diaphragm model. Rather, this mic has a pair of 22mm (medium-diaphragm) cardioid capsules in a fixed 90&deg; pickup pattern. See also the MXL 990 Stereo, which appears to be the same microphone in a different body style.</p><p>The V63M Stereo, like its large-diaphragm namesake, is a relatively high-noise microphone. It is rated at 20dBA. (The 990 Stereo mic&#8217;s specs are contradictory; it is rated both at 14dBA and 20dBA.)</p><p>The mic ships with a ring mount (MXL p/n MT-001) and a 10&#39; &#8220;Y&#8221; cable to split the mic&#8217;s 5-pin stereo output into twin 3-pin XLRM outputs. Like the non-stereo V63M, the Stereo mic also fits into MXL&#8217;s 57, USM-001, and USM-002 shockmounts.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/MXL/V63M-Stereo">MXL V63M-Stereo</a></p>
